      { question: "Why six months for the emergency fund?", answer: "It keeps you from selling investments at a loss after a job loss or a big bill. Three months can be enough with a secure job; more if your income is irregular." },
      { question: "Why does the order of accounts matter?", answer: "Tax-advantaged accounts such as Korea's pension savings and IRP, Japan's iDeCo and NISA or France's PER return part of what you pay in through tax relief, so filling them first raises your effective return. Money you may need soon should stay accessible." },
      { question: "Can I use the result for another country?", answer: "Yes. Pick the country at the top; minimum wage, minimum income, account caps and savings goals switch to that country's rules and currency." },
